Hallow as the company in hallow.exe's file properties

Explorer's file properties and Task Manager show the executables'
CompanyName. Hallow is built from Firefox but not by Mozilla, so its
executables name Hallow; the copyright and trademark lines, which credit
Firefox and Mozilla, stay.

diff --git a/browser/app/module.ver b/browser/app/module.ver
index 5ef8d2a..9d7bc60 100644
--- a/browser/app/module.ver
+++ b/browser/app/module.ver
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Mozilla Corporation
+WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Hallow
 WIN32_MODULE_COPYRIGHT=©Firefox and Mozilla Developers; available under the MPL 2 license.
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION=@MOZ_APP_WINVERSION@
 WIN32_MODULE_PRODUCTVERSION_STRING=@MOZ_APP_VERSION@
diff --git a/browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver b/browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver
index 5ef8d2a..9d7bc60 100644
--- a/browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver
+++ b/browser/app/pbproxy/module.ver
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Mozilla Corporation
+WIN32_MODULE_COMPANYNAME=Hallow
 WIN32_MODULE_COPYRIGHT=©Firefox and Mozilla Developers; available under the MPL 2 license.
